# Crude hypothesis patch B -- NOT a correct fix.
#
# Purpose: demonstrate that DEFINITION.verify.sh turns green via a SECOND,
# genuinely different mechanism from hypothesis.patch.
#
# Shape comparison vs. hypothesis.patch:
#   hypothesis.patch  -- modifies validation.py (Python, the rule checker)
#                        WIDENS the rule to also accept loop_restart edges
#                        operation: adds code to the checker
#   hypothesis_b.patch -- modifies examples/pipelines/00-convergence-loop.dot (DOT data)
#                         TEACHES the data to satisfy the existing rule as-is
#                         operation: adds retry_target="implement" attribute to test_gate
#
# Opposite polarity:
#   A fixes the rule so it accepts the example.
#   B fixes the example so it satisfies the rule.
#
# Different file, different language (DOT vs. Python), different operation
# (attribute addition vs. boolean expression widening), opposite direction.
#
# Why this is "crude": adding retry_target="implement" to the test_gate node
# in the tutorial DOT is misleading -- it implies that retry_target is required
# alongside loop_restart="true", which is not the intended teaching pattern.
# The example deliberately uses the edge-based retry idiom without a redundant
# retry_target attribute.  This patch silences the warning by satisfying the
# attribute check, not by making the code correct.
#
# Mechanism:
#   _check_goal_gate_has_retry computes:
#       has_retry = bool(node.attrs.get("retry_target") or ...)
#   Adding retry_target="implement" makes node.attrs.get("retry_target")
#   return "implement" (truthy), so has_retry is True and no WARNING is emitted.
#   _check_retry_target_exists also checks that the target node exists --
#   "implement" is a valid node ID in the graph, so no additional diagnostic fires.
#
# Verified at SHA 44428ab67a530f23aa5579104f4ff68e4e809c37:
#   - DEFINITION.verify.sh exits 0 with patch applied
#   - 87 test_validation.py tests pass (validation.py is not modified)
#   - 30 test_examples_lint_clean.py tests pass (no ERROR-severity findings)
#   - lint() on 00-convergence-loop.dot emits 0 diagnostics
#   - Tree hard-reset to 44428ab after verification; gate confirmed red again
#
# Apply via:
#   git apply .ai/hypothesis_b.patch
# from the repo root.
diff --git a/examples/pipelines/00-convergence-loop.dot b/examples/pipelines/00-convergence-loop.dot
index b2d7582..fc266dc 100644
--- a/examples/pipelines/00-convergence-loop.dot
+++ b/examples/pipelines/00-convergence-loop.dot
@@ -58,7 +58,8 @@ digraph convergence_loop {
         shape=parallelogram,
         label="pytest",
         tool_command="pytest -q test_word_counter.py > test_output.txt 2>&1 && echo gate_pass || echo gate_fail",
-        goal_gate=true
+        goal_gate=true,
+        retry_target="implement"
     ]
 
     // --- Exit ---
